{"title":"2011 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/3/6733410285a10a074e563b2e759cad30fe1412f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{8}{12} = \\frac{\\framebox {}}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"64\" height=\"38\" />, then the value represented by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/b/21b7ae5c31f138a27a58d70024be2f347e26ad44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\framebox {}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"13\" height=\"13\" /> is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/c/e6cf5fc753300e00133b2b81c5d7ee444fd71fa1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\  24\\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 1\\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 12\\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 2\\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"406\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/5/235820ed89f9ed54954565f6f7e529e091874bde.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{12}{3} = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"55\" height=\"37\" />, meaning we can divide the numerator and denominator by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to arrive at our answer.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/d/17de5b1949148d19cc5190deaefa6d6bacfb4f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{8}{12} = \\frac{8 \\div 4}{12 \\div 4} = \\frac{2}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"139\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p>Since the numerator is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and we have the same denominator, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/5/665af9ae2633b3d26a4f2bd22fe77b78442029af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(D) }2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"58\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"2011 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">2011 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2011 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2011 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First Problem</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2011 CEMC Gauss (Gra